                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15818
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Task
          Components: consumer
            Reporter: Philip Nee


In the network thread, we need a timer configure to take MAX_POLL_INTERVAL_=
MAX.=C2=A0 The reason is if the user don't poll the consumer within the int=
ernal, the member needs to leave the group.

=C2=A0

Currently, we send an acknowledgement event to the network thread per poll.=
=C2=A0 It needs to do two things 1. update autocommit state 2. update max p=
oll interval timer=C2=A0

=C2=A0

The current logic looks like this:
{code:java}
 if (heartbeat.pollTimeoutExpired(now)) {
    // the poll timeout has expired, which means that the foreground thread=
 has stalled
    // in between calls to poll().
    log.warn("consumer poll timeout has expired. This means the time betwee=
n subsequent calls to poll() " +
        "was longer than the configured max.poll.interval.ms, which typical=
ly implies that " +
        "the poll loop is spending too much time processing messages. You c=
an address this " +
        "either by increasing max.poll.interval.ms or by reducing the maxim=
um size of batches " +
        "returned in poll() with max.poll.records.");

    maybeLeaveGroup("consumer poll timeout has expired.");
} {code}



