Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-15826) WorkerSinkTask leaks Consumer if
 plugin start or stop blocks indefinitely
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Greg Harris created KAFKA-15826:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: WorkerSinkTask leaks Consumer if plugin start or stop=
 blocks indefinitely
                 Key: KAFKA-15826
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15826
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: KafkaConnect
    Affects Versions: 3.6.0
            Reporter: Greg Harris
            Assignee: Greg Harris


The WorkerSourceTask cancel() method closes the Producer, releasing it's re=
sources. The WorkerSInkTask does not do the same for the Consumer, as it do=
es not override the cancel() method.

WorkerSinkTask should close the consumer if the task is cancelled, as progr=
ess for a cancelled task will be discarded anyway.=C2=A0



