Hey De Gao,

The controller is the one that always elects a new leader. When that happens=
 that metadata is changed on the controller and once committed it=E2=80=99s b=
roadcast to all brokers in the cluster. In KRaft this would be via a Partito=
nChange record that each broker will fetch from the controller. In ZK it=E2=80=
=99d be via an RPC from the controller to the broker.=20

In either case each broker might get the notification at a different time. N=
o ordering guarantee among the brokers. But eventually they=E2=80=99ll all k=
now the new leader which means eventually the Produce will fail with NotLead=
er and the client will refresh its metadata and find out the new one.=20

In between all that leadership movement, there are various ways messages can=
 get duplicated or lost. However if you use the idempotent producer I believ=
e you actually won=E2=80=99t see dupes or missing messages so if that=E2=80=99=
s an important requirement you could look into that. The producer is designe=
d to retry in general and when you use the idempotent producer some extra me=
tadata is sent around to dedupe any messages server-side that were sent mult=
iple times by the client.=20

If you=E2=80=99re interested in learning more Kafka internals I highly recom=
mend this blog series https://www.confluent.io/blog/apache-kafka-architectur=
e-and-internals-by-jun-rao/

Hope that helped a bit.=20

Andy=20

Sent from my iPhone

> On Nov 20, 2023, at 2:07 AM, De Gao <DGao@live.co.uk> wrote:
>=20
> =EF=BB=BFHi all I have a interesting question here.
>=20
> Let's say we have 2 broker B1 B2, controller C and producer P1, P2...Pn. C=
urrently B1 holds the partition leader and Px is constantly producing messag=
es to B1. We want to move the partition leadership to B2. How does the leade=
rship change synced between B1, B2, C, and Px that it is guaranteed that all=
 the parties acknowledged the leadership change in the right order? Was ther=
e a break of produce flow in between? Any chance of  message lost?
>=20
> Thanks
>=20
> De Gao

--Apple-Mail-A3B8D925-E5B8-4352-AAC2-B87817C1BCCD--

