Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Philip Nee created KAFKA-15867:
----------------------------------

             Summary: Should ConsumerNetworkThread wrap the exception and n=
otify the polling thread?
                 Key: KAFKA-15867
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15867
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: consumer
            Reporter: Philip Nee


The ConsumerNetworkThread runs a tight loop infinitely.=C2=A0 However, when=
 encountering an unexpected exception, it logs an error and continues.

=C2=A0

I think this might not be ideal because user can run blind for a long time =
before discovering there's something wrong with the code; so I believe we s=
hould propagate the throwable back to the polling thread.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

cc [~lucasbru]=C2=A0



--
