Philip Nee resolved KAFKA-15836.
--------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

PR merged.

> KafkaConsumer subscribes to multiple topics does not respect max.poll.rec=
ords
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
----
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-15836
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15836
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>    Affects Versions: 3.7.0
>            Reporter: Philip Nee
>            Assignee: Andrew Schofield
>            Priority: Blocker
>              Labels: consumer
>             Fix For: 3.7.0
>
>
> We discovered that when KafkaConsumer subscribes to multiple topics with =
max.poll.record configured.=C2=A0 The max.poll.record is not properly respe=
cted for all poll() invocation.
> =C2=A0
> I was able to reproduce it with the AK example, here is how I ran my test=
s:
> [https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/14772]
> =C2=A0
> 1. start zookeeper and kafka server (or kraft mode should be fine too)
> 2. Run: examples/bin/java-producer-consumer-demo.sh 10000000
> 3. Polled records > 400 will be printed to stdout
> =C2=A0
> Here is what the program does:
> The produce produces a large number of records to multiple topics.=C2=A0 =
We configure the consumer using a max.poll.record =3D 400, and subscribed t=
o multiple topics.=C2=A0 The consumer poll, and the returned records can so=
metimes be larger than 400.
> =C2=A0
> This is an issue in AK 3.6 but 3.5 was fine.
> =C2=A0



