> > parity, we are opening the door to leaving a chunk of Apache Kafka=20
> > users without an easy way to upgrade to 4.0.
> > In pro of making upgrades as smooth as possible, I propose to have a=20
> > Kafka version where KIP-853 is merged and Zookeeper still is supported.=20
> > This will enable community members who can't migrate yet to KRaft to do=20
> > so in a safe way (rolling back is something goes wrong). Additionally,=20
