Hey De Gao,

Message loss or duplication can actually happen even without a leadership ch=
ange for a partition. For example if there are network issues and the produc=
er never gets the ack from the server, it=E2=80=99ll retry and cause duplica=
tes. Message loss can usually occur when you use acks=3D1 config - mostly yo=
u=E2=80=99d lose after a leadership change but in theory if the leader was r=
estarted, the page cache was lost and it stayed leader again we could lose t=
he message if it wasn=E2=80=99t replicated soon enough.=20

You might be right it=E2=80=99s more likely to occur during leadership chang=
e though - not 100% sure myself on that.=20

Point being, the idempotent producer really is the way to write once and onl=
y once as far as I=E2=80=99m aware.=20

If you have any suggestions for improvements I=E2=80=99m sure the community w=
ould love to hear them! It=E2=80=99s possible there are ways to make leaders=
hip changes more seamless and at least reduce the probability of duplicates o=
r loss. Not sure myself. I=E2=80=99ve wondered before if the older leader co=
uld reroute messages for a small period of time until the client knew the ne=
w leader for example.=20

Andrew=20

