{code:java}
// code placeholder
{code}
h1. Overview
 * This issue pertains to [SASL/OAUTHBEARER|https://kafka.apache.org/docume=
ntation/#security_sasl_oauthbearer] mechanism of Kafka authentication.=C2=
=A0
 * Kafka clients can use [SASL/OAUTHBEARER =C2=A0|https://kafka.apache.org/=
documentation/#security_sasl_oauthbearer]mechanism by overriding the [custo=
m call back handlers|https://kafka.apache.org/documentation/#security_sasl_=
oauthbearer_prod] .=C2=A0
 * [KIP-768|https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageI=
d=3D186877575] available from v3.1 =C2=A0further extends the mechanism with=
 a production grade implementation.=C2=A0
 * Kafka's [SASL/OAUTHBEARER|https://kafka.apache.org/documentation/#securi=
ty_sasl_oauthbearer] =C2=A0mechanism currently {*}rejects the non-JWT (i.e.=
 opaque) tokens{*}. This is because of a more restrictive set of characters=
 than what [RFC-6750|https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6750#section-=
2.1] recommends.=C2=A0
 * This JIRA can be considered an extension of [KIP-768|https://cwiki.apach=
e.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=3D186877575] to support the o=
paque tokens as well apart from the JWT tokens.

In summary the following character set should be supported as per the RFC -=
=C2=A0
{code:java}
1*( ALPHA / DIGIT /
                       "-" / "." / "_" / "~" / "+" / "/" ) *"=3D"
{code}
