ConsumerTestBuilder is meant to be an unit testing utility; however, we see=
m to use Mockito#spy quite liberally.=C2=A0 This is not the right testing s=
trategy because we basically turn unit testing into integration testing.

=C2=A0

While the current unit tests run fine, we should probably make the mocking =
using Mockito#mock by default and test each dependency independently.

=C2=A0

The ask here is
 # Make mock(class) by default
 # Provide more flexible interface for the testBuilder to allow user to con=
figure spy or mock.=C2=A0 Or, let user pass in their own mock.



