Philip Nee created KAFKA-15948:
----------------------------------

             Summary: Refactor AsyncKafkaConsumer shutdown
                 Key: KAFKA-15948
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15948
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: consumer
            Reporter: Philip Nee


Upon closing we need a round trip from the network thread to the applicatio=
n thread and then back to the network thread to complete the callback invoc=
ation.=C2=A0 Currently, we don't have any of that.=C2=A0 I think we need to=
 refactor our closing mechanism.=C2=A0 There are a few points to the refact=
or:
 # The network thread should know if there's a custom user callback to trig=
ger or not.=C2=A0 If there is, it should wait for the callback completion t=
o send a leave group.=C2=A0 If not, it should proceed with the shutdown.
 # The application thread sends a closing signal to the network thread and =
continuously polls the background event handler until time runs out.

=C2=A0



